#   -----------------------------------------------------------------
#   T4 : weight-shift path exposes the stored weight
#   -----------------------------------------------------------------
#     step     | wl vld   a_in      psum_in |  a_out vld_o      psum_out |      expected
#     ---------+------------------------------+------------------------------+--------------
#     T4-ld1   |  1   0      0           -3 |      0     0            -3 |            -3
#     during wload, psum_out = 0xfffffffd = -3 (weight sign-extended to 32 bits)
#     T4-ld2   |  1   0      0            0 |      0     0             0 |             0
#     feeding a second weight immediately replaces what the mux shows;
#     this combinational path is what makes a column a shift register.
#     T4 ends: 8 checks, 0 errors  [PASS]
